# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run a managed workflow one time for each set of inputs, collect the results, and stay under the active job limit."
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng managed workflow nang isang beses para sa bawat set ng input, kolektahin ang mga resulta, at manatili sa ilalim ng active job limit."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run a parameter sweep"
msgstr "Magpatakbo ng parameter sweep"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/run-parameter-sweep.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mga bersyon ng package\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang code sa pahinang ito ay binuo gamit ang mga sumusunod na requirement.\n"
"Inirerekomenda naming gamitin ang mga bersyong ito o mas bago.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A parameter sweep works like a Slurm job array. Call `run()` one time for each set of inputs, and the jobs run at the same time, each on its own node. Use the same pattern for any batch of independent inputs, such as one job for each molecule or each backend. Jobs cannot send data to each other, so split the work into independent inputs.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Ang parameter sweep ay gumagana tulad ng Slurm job array. Tawagin ang `run()` nang isang beses para sa bawat set ng input, at sabay-sabay na tatakbo ang mga job, bawat isa sa sarili nitong node. Gamitin ang parehong pattern para sa anumang batch ng mga independent na input, tulad ng isang job para sa bawat molecule o bawat backend. Hindi makakapagpadala ng data sa isa't isa ang mga job, kaya hatiin ang trabaho sa mga independent na input.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The examples on this page use the workflow from [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow), which reads one angle, `theta`:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga halimbawa sa pahinang ito ay gumagamit ng workflow mula sa [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow), na nagbabasa ng isang anggulo, `theta`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start the jobs {#start-the-jobs}"
msgstr "Simulan ang mga job {#start-the-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Get the workflow by its title, and call `run()` one time for each input. Save the job IDs to a file:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunin ang workflow gamit ang title nito, at tawagin ang `run()` nang isang beses para sa bawat input. I-save ang mga job ID sa isang file:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Check every input first.** If the workflow has an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), call `validate_arguments()` on each input before the loop.\n"
msgstr "**Suriin muna ang bawat input.** Kung may [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema) ang workflow, tawagin ang `validate_arguments()` sa bawat input bago ang loop.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Save the job IDs to a file.** You can then collect the results from a new session.\n"
msgstr "**I-save ang mga job ID sa isang file.** Makokolekta mo na ang mga resulta mula sa bagong session.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Give each run's files a unique name.** All runs share the workflow's file storage. See [Best practice: give each run's files a unique name](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name).\n"
msgstr "**Bigyan ng natatanging pangalan ang mga file ng bawat run.** Nagbabahagi ang lahat ng run ng file storage ng workflow. Tingnan ang [Best practice: give each run's files a unique name](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Stay under the [active job limit](#active-job-limit).** A managed workflow does not queue jobs over the limit, so when you reach it, start more jobs only after earlier jobs end.\n"
msgstr "**Manatili sa ilalim ng [active job limit](#active-job-limit).** Hindi nagq-queue ng mga job na lampas sa limit ang managed workflow, kaya kapag naabot mo ito, magsimula ng mas marami pang job pagkatapos lang matapos ang mga naunang job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collect the results {#collect-the-results}"
msgstr "Kolektahin ang mga resulta {#collect-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Get each job by its ID, and catch failed jobs so that one failure does not stop the loop:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunin ang bawat job gamit ang ID nito, at saluhin ang mga pumalyang job para hindi huminto ang loop dahil sa isang pagkabigo:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To rerun the inputs that failed, call `run()` again with the same arguments.\n"
msgstr "Para patakbuhin ulit ang mga input na pumalya, tawagin ulit ang `run()` gamit ang parehong mga argumento.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Active job limit {#active-job-limit}"
msgstr "Limitasyon sa aktibong job {#active-job-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can have up to 50 jobs that are queued, initializing, running, or canceling at the same time. This limit counts all of your jobs, including jobs of other workflows. If you exceed this limit, `run()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException` and does not create or queue the job:\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang magkaroon ng hanggang 50 job na naka-queue, nag-i-initialize, tumatakbo, o kinakansela nang sabay-sabay. Binibilang ng limitasyong ito ang lahat ng job mo, kasama ang mga job ng ibang workflow. Kapag lumampas ka sa limitasyong ito, nagtataas ang `run()` ng `QiskitServerlessException` at hindi gumagawa o nagku-queue ng job:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) to share input files between runs and give each run's files a unique name.\n"
"- [Choose a compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) to run each job of the sweep on a size that matches its input.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Mga rekomendasyon\">\n"
"- [Pamahalaan ang mga file sa iba't ibang run](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) para magbahagi ng mga input file sa pagitan ng mga run at bigyan ng natatanging pangalan ang mga file ng bawat run.\n"
"- [Pumili ng compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) para patakbuhin ang bawat job ng sweep sa laking tugma sa input nito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
